WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.667
Langfuse.

2
00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:07.500
Open-source observability built for LLM apps, so you can see inside every request.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.500
Every request becomes a trace.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:17.333
Each pipeline stage inside it, like retrieval, rerank, generation, or a tool call, becomes a span.

5
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:21.767
Generation spans also record the model, token counts, and cost.

6
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:24.933
Here's a request laid out by stage.

7
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:26.433
Retrieval is quick.

8
00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:28.840
Rerank is far wider than the rest.

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.567
The widest span is where your latency lives.

10
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.967
Langfuse adds LLM-specific layers on top.

11
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.933
It starts with the raw traces.

12
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:40.833
User feedback attaches to those traces.

13
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.733
Prompts are versioned and linked.

14
00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.308
And eval scores are stored per trace.

15
00:00:45.308 --> 00:00:51.333
Which prompt version caused the bad answers users flagged becomes a query, not an archaeology dig.

16
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:54.467
Instrumenting is a decorator.

17
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:58.733
Put observe on retrieve and rerank, and each call becomes a span.

18
00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:03.933
Mark generate as a generation, so it records the model, tokens, and cost.

19
00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:07.033
The outer rag function becomes the parent trace.

20
00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:11.376
You self-host Langfuse and decorate four functions.

21
00:01:11.376 --> 00:01:13.533
Within the hour, three discoveries.

22
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:18.906
First, the reranker is two point eight seconds of a three point nine second median.

23
00:01:18.906 --> 00:01:20.433
You were blaming the LLM.

24
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:27.055
Second, sorting by cost reveals one agent loop asking the same question forty times a day.

25
00:01:27.055 --> 00:01:28.600
Hello, semantic cache.

26
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:35.533
Third, nightly eval scores land on traces, so thumbs down plus low faithfulness becomes your triage queue.

27
00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:37.527
Let's recap.

28
00:01:37.527 --> 00:01:40.633
A request is a trace, and each stage is a span.

29
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:44.200
Generation spans record model, tokens, and cost.

30
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.333
Feedback, prompt versions, and eval scores hang off the traces.

31
00:01:48.633 --> 00:01:52.850
And it is self-hostable, so regulated teams keep their data.

32
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.467
Next up: OpenTelemetry.
